  "id": "04-per-godown-positions",
  "description": "The same item in two godowns is TWO positions carrying two different average costs, never one blended one. A single purchase receives 10 @ 100.0000 into Main Location (line 1) and 5 @ 150.0000 into Warehouse B (line 2); a single sale ships 3 from Main and 1 from Warehouse B. Main: 1000.0000 in, 3*100.0000 = 300.0000 out, closing 7.0000 / 700.0000 @ 100.0000. Warehouse B: 750.0000 in, 1*150.0000 = 150.0000 out, closing 4.0000 / 600.0000 @ 150.0000. Total closing value 1300.0000. Blending the godowns away would give one pool of 15.0000 @ 1750.0000 = 116.666667/unit, cost the four issued units 466.6667 instead of 450.0000 and leave a closing value of 1283.3333 - so the dimension is not cosmetic, it changes the money.",
